mation(.spring)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (native)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" body."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"How the categories map","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"How-the-categories-map"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patches"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"type":"text","text":", interpolation, logic — carry no state. They run an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input through math and emit a result, which is exactly a computed property or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inline expression."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" exposes discrete outputs: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"text":". Each becomes a SwiftUI gesture whose result lands in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" or fires a callback. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".interaction(…)"},{"text":" modifier attaches only the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recognizers you ask for, so gesture arbitration stays clean.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"State and memory","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pop Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — remember a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between evaluations. That is what ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is for; the update path is a gesture","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"callback, an ","type":"text"},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or an assignment.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Animation","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"Classic Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Pop Animation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — drives a value toward a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"target over time, which is a state change wrapped in ","type":"text"},{"code":"withAnimation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".animation(_:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One naming note: Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition"},{"text":" means ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"interpolation","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (mapping one range","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"onto another), not SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".transition()"},{"text":" modifier for view insertion and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"removal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"When a mapping isn’t exact","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"When-a-mapping-isnt-exact"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some Origami semantics have no direct SwiftUI equivalent — continuous-time springs,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"custom JavaScript patches, absolute-position layout. Rather than approximate them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"silently, each t